{"seq":3,"slug":"fate-exposure","title":"环境归趋与暴露","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"transport-transformation","title":"环境迁移与转化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/transport-transformation","wordCount":1891,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"bioaccumulation","title":"生物富集与放大","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/bioaccumulation","wordCount":1883,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"exposure-assessment","title":"暴露评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/fate-exposure/exposure-assessment","wordCount":1752,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"环境归趋与暴露\">环境归趋与暴露</h1><p>知道一种污染物有多毒（基础章）、知道它是什么（污染物章），还不足以判断风险——因为风险取决于它实际去了哪、变成了什么、最终有多少进入了某个受体的体内。这一章把污染物的固有属性，翻译成它在真实环境中的行为与人和生物的实际接触量，是连接「物质毒性」与「风险结论」之间不可省略的桥梁。</p>\n<p>第一篇「环境迁移与转化」追踪污染物在大气、水、土壤、生物四种介质之间的分配（由 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{ow}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>、<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{oc}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">oc</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>、<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_{aw}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 等分配系数决定）、介质内的输运（平流、扩散、弥散），以及光解、水解、生物降解等转化过程。它解释了为什么 POPs 能全球迁移、为什么降解产物有时比母体更毒，并以多介质逸度模型整合全部过程。</p>\n<p>第二篇「生物富集与放大」讲污染物如何沿食物链层层浓缩。生物浓缩、生物蓄积、生物放大三个概念被严格区分，BCF、BAF、BMF、TMF 等指标量化富集潜力。它揭示了为什么北极熊体内的 POPs 浓度能比海水高千万倍、为什么顶级掠食者（包括人类）最危险。</p>\n<p>第三篇「暴露评估」把前两篇给出的各介质浓度，转化为「某个具体受体实际接触并吸收了多少」。外暴露法（浓度乘接触参数）与生物监测（直接测体内浓度）两条路线互为印证，并延伸到暴露组与高通量暴露预测的前沿。</p>\n<p>三篇层层递进，最终输出的暴露量正是下一章生态与人体风险评估的直接输入。</p>\n"}